<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>info about AK2365A: <a href="https://www.alldatasheet.com/datasheet-pdf/view/780938/AKM/AK2365A.html" class="postlink">https://www.alldatasheet.com/datasheet- ... 2365A.html</a></div></blockquote>//this function initialises the AK2365A IF Chip in V1-V4 Radios for the specified band and bandwidth and needs to be called whenever the receiver is turned on.<br>1?  Does the V5 also use AK2365A IF chip?<br>2 )  Another question: Does the MD-9600 use the C6000 to demodulate the FM, not through the IF chip?<br>Thanks!</div></blockquote>1. The V5 (aka V4A) radios do not use the same IF chip as previous versions.<br>I can't remember the part number of the IF chip, but it is NOT configurable via an SPI interface. <br>It simply has a control signal to allow bandwidth to be selected (Wide / Narrow)<br><br>Look at the souce code in the file radioHardwareInterface.c<br><br>2. Yes</div></blockquote>OK?Thanks!<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6826">BA7IQE</a> — Mon Jun 09, 2025 7:49 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
